Figure 2:Overview ofOrg-Agent.Given user inputs, interaction history, and organizational constraints,
❶TDG constructiondecomposes the task into subtasks and represents their dependencies in a Task Dependency Graph;
❷dependency-aware schedulingorders the nodes through topological sorting;
and ❸constraint-aware node executionuses the LLM to determine and take actions toward node objectives based on the assembled execution context, with evidence-acquisition tools providing relevant records and memory-management tools supplying memory for context assembly and updating it with information from actions and observations.
